From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fish <fish@bc250-fsr4-research>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] radv: BC-250 FSR4 combined-unroll selection (2.84)

Downstream FSR4 optimization from the BC-250 research kit dated
2026-09-06, rebased onto our existing series. This is the delta between
that kit's "accepted 2.84" checkpoint and our patches 0001-0005; the
parts of that checkpoint we already carry (gfx1013 enablement, mesh/task
shaders, the V3 deferred SDot lowering) are excluded.

NIR-level pattern matching and rematerialization over FSR4's dot and
convolution loops: grouped dots, loop/cooperative rematerialization,
pointwise column streaming and the September 6 combined-unroll
selection. Rewrites are gated on exact shader identity -- the
bc250_*_expected[] tables verify the incoming shader's constants before
any bc250_*_prepacked[] replacement is used -- so a shader that does not
match is left untouched.

Also carries two supporting changes the above depends on: correct NIR
metadata invalidation in ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt(), and
separation of the FSR4 pipeline cache key so cached shaders cannot be
served across BC250_FSR4_DISABLE settings.

Measured by the kit at 8.015 ms -> 5.843 ms per FSR4.1.1 INT8 upscale
(1506x848 -> 2560x1440 Balanced, 40 CU @ 1850 MHz): 2.172 ms, 27.1%.

Origin: bc250-fsr4-20260906 research kit, source/accepted-2.84.patch
---
diff --git a/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt.c b/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt.c
index 2d091a7d7cb..13790ab4adc 100644
--- a/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt.c
@@ -118,5 +118,5 @@ ac_nir_fixup_smem_loads_null_prt(nir_shader *nir, uint8_t address_prt_wa_control
       .control_bit = address_prt_wa_control_bit,
    };
 
-   return nir_shader_intrinsics_pass(nir, fixup_smem_loads_null_prt, nir_metadata_all, &s);
+   return nir_shader_intrinsics_pass(nir, fixup_smem_loads_null_prt, nir_metadata_control_flow, &s);
 }
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
index ab281a1894c..c4c4abfb991 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
@@ -363,6 +363,11 @@ radv_device_get_cache_uuid(struct radv_physical_device *pdev, void *uuid)
       return -1;
 #endif
 
+   /* Separate production and fallback disk/application pipeline caches. */
+   const char *bc250_fsr4_cache = debug_get_bool_option("BC250_FSR4_DISABLE", false) ?
+      "bc250-fsr4-integrated-v2-disabled" : "bc250-fsr4-integrated-v2";
+   _mesa_blake3_update(&ctx, bc250_fsr4_cache, strlen(bc250_fsr4_cache));
+
    _mesa_blake3_final(&ctx, blake3);
 
    memcpy(uuid, blake3, VK_UUID_SIZE);
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_shader.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_shader.c
index 4f0d30ea28b..d1d61670ca1 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_shader.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_shader.c
@@ -178,6 +178,10260 @@ radv_can_dump_shader_stats(const struct radv_compiler_info *compiler_info, nir_s
  * signed dot instructions are eligible. This leaves ED7 (2048), 0d64 (512)
  * and the short 20-dot kernels on the B2 path.
  */
+/* BC250 FSR4 integration v2 — exact arithmetic, enabled by default.
+ * The September 6 combined-unroll selection, with full shader identity gates.
+ * Every loaded-weight specialization verifies all consumed coefficients and
+ * preserves the original fallback. Signed-byte bounds and wrapping i32 bases
+ * are unchanged. Explicit subgroup restrictions retain precedence.
+ */
+struct bc250_fsr4_counts { unsigned dots, constant_dots, zero_acc; };
+
+enum bc250_fsr4_dot_mode { BC250_FSR4_FIXED, BC250_FSR4_CHAIN, BC250_FSR4_CHAIN2 };
+
+struct bc250_group_options { unsigned limit, groups, dots; };
+
+struct bc250_dynamic_column {
+   nir_alu_instr *tails[32];
+   nir_alu_src inputs[32], base;
+   uint32_t weights[32];
+   unsigned count;
+};
+
+struct bc250_dynamic_columns {
+   struct bc250_dynamic_column *columns;
+   unsigned count;
+};
+
+struct bc250_stream_column {
+   nir_alu_src inputs[36], base;
+   uint32_t weights[36];
+   nir_alu_instr *tail;
+};
+
+struct bc250_stream_columns {
+   struct bc250_stream_column columns[16];
+   unsigned count;
+   bool excess;
+};
+
+struct bc250_point_column {
+   nir_alu_src inputs[16], base;
+   uint32_t weights[16];
+   nir_alu_instr *tail;
+   unsigned length;
+};
+
+struct bc250_point_set {
+   struct bc250_point_column columns[16];
+   unsigned count, limit;
+};
+
+struct bc250_guard_column {
+   nir_alu_instr *chain[32]; /* tail first */
+   unsigned length;
+};
+
+struct bc250_guard_columns {
+   struct bc250_guard_column columns[64];
+   unsigned count;
+   bool invalid;
+};
+
+struct bc250_coop_remat {
+   nir_builder *b;
+   nir_block *body, *before;
+   struct hash_table *map;
+   unsigned depth;
+};
+
+struct bc250_loop_remat {
+   nir_builder *b;
+   struct set *available;
+   struct hash_table *map;
+   unsigned depth;
+};
+
+struct bc250_e288_groups {
+   int previous[336], first[336];
+   bool tail[336];
+   unsigned count;
+};
+
+struct bc250_neighbor_groups {
+   int previous[336], first[336];
+   bool tail[336];
+   unsigned count;
+};
+
+struct bc250_nested_groups {
+   int previous[400], first[400];
+   bool tail[400];
+   unsigned count;
+};
+
+struct bc250_nested_context {
+   nir_def *phis[3];
+   unsigned trips[3], count, columns;
+};
